## Combined Figure

The two panels are joined with patchwork. The y-axis title appears only on the
left panel; the positive panel suppresses its left axis to avoid duplication.

```{r}
#| label: fig-zscore-combined
#| fig-width: 6.5
#| fig-height: 4.5

p_zneg_trim <- p_zneg +
  theme(plot.margin = margin(4, 0, 8, 4))

p_zpos_trim <- p_zpos +
  theme(
    axis.title.y.left = element_blank(),
    axis.text.y.left  = element_blank(),
    axis.ticks.y.left = element_blank(),
    plot.margin       = margin(4, 8, 8, 2)
  )

combined_z <- (p_zneg_trim + p_zpos_trim) +
  plot_layout(guides = "collect", widths = c(11, 5)) &
  theme(
    legend.position  = "bottom",
    panel.background = element_rect(fill = NA, color = NA),
    plot.background  = element_rect(fill = NA, color = NA),
    legend.text      = element_text(size = legend_text_size, family = plot_font),
    legend.key.size  = unit(0.35, "cm"),
    axis.line        = element_line(linewidth = 0.5)
  )
combined_z <- combined_z & guides(fill = guide_legend(nrow = 2))

combined_z

ggsave(
  filename = file.path(fig_indicator, "zscore_profile_combined.png"),
  device   = "png",
  plot     = combined_z,
  width    = 6.5, height = 4.5, dpi = fig_dpi, units = "in",
  bg       = "transparent"
)
```
